# .NET build output. These were tracked, which meant every local test run
# dirtied the working tree with rebuilt binaries and a latency number that
# moves by a millisecond — noise in every diff, and a stop-hook nag after
# every verification pass. Nothing depends on the committed copies: CI builds
# the tools from source (`dotnet run --project ...`).
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Unity's generated folders, for the same reason.
ledger/Library/
ledger/Temp/
ledger/Logs/
ledger/UserSettings/

# Local self-test output.
ledger/sim-out/
sim-run/

# TTS benchmark: per-engine venvs, downloaded models, generated audio. Multi-GB
# and machine-specific — the script rebuilds all of it on demand.
tools/tts-benchmark/.venv-*/
tools/tts-benchmark/models/
tools/tts-benchmark/refs/
tools/tts-benchmark/ledger-tts-out/

# Python scratch.
__pycache__/

# Scratch from the deliberate-break runner. It restores via atexit, but a
# hard kill can leave one behind and a backup of a source file must never
# be mistaken for source.
*.breakbak

# Mixamo harvest — the token is a live credential and the harvest is ~1GB.
# Neither belongs in git; the picks under ledger/Assets/Characters do.
mixamo_token.txt
ledger-mixamo/
tools/mixamo-pick/animations/
# characters_available.txt is TRACKED now, deliberately. It is the complete
# list of bodies Jafar's Mixamo account can see, and while it was ignored
# every body pick in this project was made blind, from remembered names —
# which is how a catwalk sashay and two grey mannequins got cast. The
# animation side has `_catalogue.txt` for exactly this reason.
ledger/.verify-footer

# The ONNX export probe's output — .onnx files, per-part results and the
# report itself. It is a MEASUREMENT of one machine's run, so a copy
# arriving by git is the same hazard the probe was just fixed for: a
# report that outlives the run that wrote it, landing on somebody else's
# machine looking like their answer. The selftest writes one as part of
# proving a stale report cannot survive, which is how one got committed.
tools/voice-live/export-out/
# And its sibling: the listening page `probe.py` writes for one
# machine's backends. Same class, found by grepping for it rather than
# by waiting for it to be committed too.
tools/voice-live/out/

# The two wav files "3 HEAR IT SPEAK.bat" writes — output, not source.
tools/voice-live/speak-out/

# The game graphs — about 2 GB, and they ship with the build rather than git.
tools/voice-live/game-out/
ledger/.onnx-cache/

# The watcher remembers the last job id it ran, per machine.
.pc-watcher-state.json

# JAFAR'S PYTHON ENVIRONMENT, which lives inside the repository. Never
# ignored until the watcher staged it wholesale and committed part of it.
tools/voice-live/env-export/
tools/voice-live/env/

# THE PYTHON ENVIRONMENT AND THE EXPORTED GRAPHS, AND THESE FOUR LINES WENT
# MISSING ONCE ALREADY. They were written, they were watched working, and
# they were never committed — they lived in one container's working copy
# until it was reclaimed, so every machine except that one carried on
# without them. The symptom surfaced days later as thirteen untracked
# site-packages files stopping a repair script, and the cause was invisible
# precisely because the fix HAD been seen to work.
#
# `env-export/` is Jafar's virtual environment. A wide `git add` swept part
# of it once and the next reset took the folder with it. The add is scoped
# now; this is the second lock on the same door.
#
# `game-out/` is ~4.5 GB of exported .onnx graphs, rebuilt on demand from
# the model. `speak-out/` is audio one machine generated. Both are outputs
# of a run, and the rule here for those is that they travel as a named
# report, never as whatever happened to be in the directory.
tools/voice-live/env-export/
tools/voice-live/env/
tools/voice-live/game-out/
tools/voice-live/speak-out/
production/logs/
production/scratch/
tools/runner/config.local
ledger/PerceptionGolden/bin/
ledger/PerceptionGolden/obj/
ue-probe/Binaries/
ue-probe/Intermediate/
ue-probe/Saved/
ue-probe/DerivedDataCache/
ue-probe/Packaged/
ue-probe/Saved/
ue-probe/Intermediate/
ue-probe/Binaries/
ue-probe/DerivedDataCache/
ue-probe/golden-result.txt
tools/meshgen/__pycache__/
tools/meshgen/blender/__pycache__/
